+	/*
+	 * A _TMP that reads back EXACTLY _CRT is a firmware "sensor unreadable"
+	 * sentinel, not a temperature: a working sensor reports a value strictly
+	 * below its own critical trip right up until genuine thermal failure, and
+	 * a true critical overheat is the EC's hardware cutoff (below the OS), not
+	 * tzmon's. On the ThinkPad X1 Extreme Gen5 \_TZ.THM0._TMP returns TCRT
+	 * (== _CRT == 128 C) whenever an EC level field reads 0x80 "sensor not
+	 * populated" -- confirmed on the hardware under Linux: the zone sits at
+	 * 44-48 C with one sensor pegged at -128 (0x80), while _TMP intermittently
+	 * returns 128. The zone has a single _CRT trip, no _HOT and no gradient
+	 * that can reach 128, so 128 is ALWAYS the sentinel here. Acting on it
